==Strategy==
A Cubist Crimes remake with added Li'l Doges and Zollows as replacement for [[Brollow]]s. For maximum caution, it is advised to defeat all the Li'l Doges before you start attacking the enemy base. That aside, this stage can be beaten in the exact same way as the original Cubist Crimes, which also means useful units in Cubist Crimes are useful here as well, such as [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Macho Legs]] and [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jellycat]]. The Zollow flock takes 80 seconds to spawn, which is enough time to charge the [[Ototo Corps|Curseblast]] and fire it to temporarily disable the Li'l Doges' Dodge Attack abilities, making this level a good deal easier. In the worst of cases, one can soft-reset this stage if things go sour with the Li'l Doges' dodges.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Master of Mind Soractes (Special Cat)|Master of Mind Catcrates]]: while obviously not being available for {{1c}}, Catcrates will make future replays of this stage much easier, with high enough range to avoid the Zollows' [[Omni Strike|Omnistrikes]] behind common meatshields, and being able to easily destroy the base at level 49 or higher (44 with a Sm Attack Up Combo) through his [[Conjure]] as soon as his Omnistrike's 150 forward piece locks onto the enemy base

==Trivia==
*"Tear-Soaked" may be a reference to [[Zollow]]'s Japanese description, which mentions acidic tears he has from the pain of his body being stripped of flesh. It could also refer to [[Li'l Doge]] crying about their inability to help [[Doge]].
*Tear-Soaked Puppy is the last [[Uncanny Legends]] stage to have no [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relics]].
*This stage uses a background from the [[Power Pro Baseball Collaboration Event]].

